Easy ID before opening, I guess I should have said. It's too late to bless
an open tin, after all. Knowing soldiers carried tins of beans would lead
to (Hey, that soldier had a tin, must be beans! Bless it!) as opposed to
the need to at least read an identify scroll first. Of course, this is a
bit like knowing what potions nymphs are carrying.

One advantage I could see to soldiers carrying tins of jumping beans,
though (whatever effect they're in fact given), is that they won't show up
before the soldiers do. This would lead to YA Amazing Benefit from Ludios
in those games where it existed, but the Fort is already a known, and
random, game imbalancer for all classes.

IMHO, though, not having the tin of beans appear until characters can
handle soldiers, and giving them a controlled likelihood of finding tins,
just increases the possibility that they'll have found TC before ingesting
the beans.

As for the jumping intrinsic: yes, I'm amazed I didn't think of this, nor
did the people who discussed the original YANI float the idea. I think a
return trip to the drawing board is in order....

